    "title": "What Parents Can Do When Daycare Abuse Is Suspected - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KidsInTheHouse2 ,\n8 hours ago You pick up your child and they flinch when a caregiver reaches for them, or you find a bruise with no believable explanation. Daycare is supposed to be a safe place, so those moments cut straight through the weekday routine. More parents are confronting situations where behavior changes, unexplained injuries, or sudden resistance to drop-off raise alarms and demand a clear response. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
